_issues_count":205,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["python","sql","sqlalchemy"],"visibility":"public","forks":1606,"open_issues":205,"watchers":11252,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pulls/7048","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pull/7048","diff_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pull/7048.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pull/7048.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!-- Provide a general summary of your proposed changes in the Title field above -->\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6435\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe your changes in detail -->\r\n\r\nThis PR changes mypy plugin's `extract_python_type_from_typeengine` so that it can also infer `Enum` type of the form `some_module.SomeEnum` (aka `MemberExpr` in mypy) in addition to currently supported `SomeEnum` (aka `NameExpr`).\r\nBoth `MemberExpr` and `NameExpr` are a child class of `RefExpr`, so this change looked very natural to me, even though I'm not particulary familar with mypy's internal.\r\n\r\nIn order to test a similar example to the original issue (it uses `import`), I added `__init__.py` under `test/ext/mypy/fiiles`, which might be a little bit odd. I believe I can test `MemberExpr` without actually using `import` (and thus without `__init__.py`), so if that's preferred, please let me know. I will remove it and change the testing strategy.\r\n\r\n**Thanks for the code review!**\r\n\r\n### Checklist\r\n<!-- go over following points. check them with an `x` if they do apply, (they turn into clickable checkboxes once the PR is submitted, so no need to do everything at once)\r\